            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Applicable Scenarios</h2>
<p>When managing multiple overseas advertising platforms (Meta, Google, TikTok, etc.), operations teams often encounter discrepancies between top-up amounts and platform records, spend data not matching bills, or invoice amount errors. This SOP establishes a standardized reconciliation process to reduce human errors.</p>
<h2>Step 1: Top-up Record Verification</h2>
<h3>1.1 Obtain Top-up Documentation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Record for each top-up: <strong>platform name, account ID, top-up time, amount, currency type</strong></li>
<li>Save screenshots or system notifications confirming successful top-ups</li>
<li>If topping up through an agency, retain transfer receipts and agency confirmation emails</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.2 Verify Platform Receipt</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Check Item</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Received Amount</td>
<td>Confirm account balance increase matches top-up amount</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Receipt Time</td>
<td>Record time difference between top-up and receipt (some platforms may delay)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account Attribution</td>
<td>Verify the correct account number received the funds to avoid cross-charging</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>1.3 Handle Time Zone Differences</h3>
<p>Some platforms display times in <strong>UTC</strong>. Convert to local time zone for verification. Document the conversion between local top-up time and platform-recorded UTC time.</p>
<h2>Step 2: Spend Data Reconciliation</h2>
<h3>2.1 Daily Spend Retrieval</h3>
<p>At a fixed time daily (e.g., 10:00 Beijing Time), export the previous day's spend report from each platform. Key fields: <strong>date, campaign name, spend amount, currency, account ID</strong>.</p>
<h3>2.2 Exchange Rate Handling</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Top-up rate</strong>: Record the actual exchange rate used at top-up</li>
<li><strong>Spend rate</strong>: Spend is based on the platform's settlement currency (usually USD or EUR)</li>
<li>At month-end, convert all currencies to <strong>base currency</strong> (e.g., CNY) for reporting</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip</strong>: Use fixed rates (e.g., month-start rate or contracted rate) for monthly summaries to avoid daily fluctuations affecting comparability.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.3 Periodic Spend Aggregation</h3>
<p>Aggregate spend at daily, weekly, and monthly levels:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daily spend</strong>: Track individual account pacing</li>
<li><strong>Weekly spend</strong>: Compare budget consumption progress</li>
<li><strong>Monthly spend</strong>: Reconcile with monthly invoices</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.4 Anomaly Detection</h3>
<p>Flag and investigate these situations:</p>
<ul>
<li>Daily spend increases by more than 200% compared to previous day</li>
<li>Account balance drops significantly without corresponding conversion improvement</li>
<li>A campaign's spend stalls (may trigger platform review)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Step 3: Invoice Verification</h2>
<h3>3.1 Invoice Retrieval Channels</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Invoice Path</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta</td>
<td>Business Settings → Billing → Download Invoice</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads</td>
<td>Tools → Billing → Documents</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>Ads Manager → Billing Center → Invoices</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>3.2 Key Verification Elements</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Invoice amount</strong> matches monthly spend aggregation</li>
<li><strong>Invoice抬头</strong> (company name, tax ID) is correct</li>
<li><strong>Billing period</strong> covers the complete period</li>
</ul>
<h3>3.3 Discrepancy Handling</h3>
<p>When invoice amounts differ from spend aggregation:</p>
<ol>
<li>Check for <strong>refunds, credits, or platform credits</strong> not yet recorded</li>
<li>Review <strong>unbilled spend</strong> (platforms typically have 3-5 day settlement delays)</li>
<li>Contact platform support or agency to confirm discrepancy cause</li>
<li>Note discrepancy reason and resolution in reconciliation records</li>
</ol>
<h2>Step 4: Archive Reconciliation Records</h2>
<h3>4.1 Recommended Archive Contents</h3>
<ul>
<li>Reconciliation period (start/end dates)</li>
<li>Account list with balance change details</li>
<li>Spend aggregation (with exchange rate documentation)</li>
<li>Invoice copies or digital versions</li>
<li>Discrepancy records and resolutions</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.2 Recommended Archive Schedule</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Top-up records</strong>: Update in real-time; archive all monthly records at month-end</li>
<li><strong>Spend data</strong>: Record daily; aggregate monthly</li>
<li><strong>Invoice verification</strong>: Complete previous month's invoices by the 10th of the following month</li>
</ul>
<h2>FAQ Quick Reference</h2>
<p><strong>Q: What if platform balance doesn't update immediately after top-up?</strong></p>
<p>Some platforms (especially agency-mediated top-ups) have 24-48 hour receipt delays. Retain top-up receipts and follow up with agency or platform support.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What if invoice amount is less than spend aggregation?</strong></p>
<p>Platforms may have unbilled spend from recent days, or there may be credits offsetting charges. Mark "pending billing amount" in reconciliation records and clear when next invoice arrives.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to avoid confusion when reconciling multiple accounts?</strong></p>
<p>Assign unique IDs to each ad account and use consistent ID naming across all reconciliation files to avoid errors from similar account names.</p>
<hr />
<p>This SOP can be adapted based on your team's actual platforms and financial processes. The key is establishing <strong>consistent reconciliation rhythms and anomaly handling mechanisms</strong> to ensure clear accounts and controlled risks.</p>
